<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Perón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1974</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Juan Domingo Perón</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Perón was an Argentine army officer who rose to power as labour minister after the 1943 coup and was elected president in 1946. With his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eva-peron">Eva Perón</a> he built a mass movement based on trade unions, industrialisation and social welfare. Overthrown in 1955, he lived in exile until returning to the presidency in 1973, dying in office the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-peron.jpg" alt="Juan Perón" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Domingo_Per%C3%B3n_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
